{"description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "The Cid, Corneille's masterpiece set in medieval Spain, was the first great work of French classical drama; Cinna, written three years later in 1641, is a tense political drama, while The Theatrical Illusion, an earlier work, is reminiscent of Shakespeare's exuberant comedies."}, "notes": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "Bibliography: p. 20."}, "identifiers": {"goodreads": ["213011"], "librarything": ["168832"]}, "title": "The Cid ; Cinna ; The theatrical illusion", "authors": [{"key": "/authors/OL130779A"}], "publish_date": "1975", "other_titles": ["Cid."], "publishers": ["Penguin"], "series": ["The Penguin classics"], "covers": [103870], "local_id": ["urn:phillips:31867000932538", "urn:sfpl:31223054169678", "urn:sfpl:31223054169652", "urn:bwbsku:KQ-912-303"], "lc_classifications": ["PQ1745.E5 C3 1975", "PQ1745.E5.C3 1975"], "publish_places": ["Harmondsworth"], "contributions": ["Cairncross, John."], "subjects": ["Corneille, Pierre, 1606-1684 -- Translations into English", "Cid, ca. 1043-1099 -- Drama", "Cinna, Gnaeus Cornelius -- Drama"], "pagination": "281 p. ;", "source_records": ["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part09.dat:145798352:971", "marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:70629970:1099", "marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i08.records.utf8:1882306:1177", "marc:marc_openlibraries_phillipsacademy/PANO_FOR_IA_05072019.mrc:76358837:1453", "marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run01.mrc:54291485:1950", "ia:cidcinnatheatric0000corn", "bwb:9780140443127", "marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part10.utf8:43615444:1187", "ia:cidcinnatheatric0000corn_f5k1", "promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-05-23", "marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.00.20150123.full.mrc:584081103:939", "idb:9780140443127", "marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-002.mrc:337086549:1584", "marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_016.bib.mrc:144478070:2338"], "dewey_decimal_class": ["842/.4"], "languages": [{"key": "/